sam: Heads-up: our new next-template example (edge + LlamaIndex wiring) is causing sporadic failures in the eval harness. Symptoms look like partial streams after a 401 during token rotation.

yasmin: Can you paste the server handler from the example?

sam: Here it is:
```js
export const runtime = 'edge';
export default async function api(req) {
  const { q } = await req.json();
  const res = await fetch(`${process.env.RD_API}/v1/chat`, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.RD_KEY}` },
    body: JSON.stringify({ input: q })
  });
  return new Response(await res.text(), { status: res.status });
}
```

eli: Two likely culprits: 1) edge runtime surface doesn't expose env in the same way on some hosts so Authorization can be empty, 2) the example pins an older SDK that had a refresh concurrency bug.

yasmin: Agree. Low-friction fix: bump the SDK in the template to the latest patch and add a clear guard that errors with a helpful message if the key is missing. Eg:
```js
if (!process.env.RD_KEY) throw new Error('RD_KEY missing: set .env.local or use node runtime for this route');
```

sam: Also propose we add a tiny integration test that uses msw to simulate token expiry: first request returns 401, token endpoint returns new token, next request succeeds. That would have caught it.

eli: Good plan. Please also tweak our eval harness: treat 401 as potentially transient during rotation and retry with exponential backoff up to 3 times before failing. Right now the harness flags truncation immediately.

ci-bot: Created issue #2634: "next-template: edge auth rotation can cause transient 401 and truncated eval output" assigned to yasmin 0 https://issues.internal/2634

qa-bot: Marked CI job flaky: examples/next-template-eval (run 1098). Re-run after PR merge.

yasmin: I'll open a PR to bump the sdk, add the env guard, and include msw test. Will also add a short note in README called "Edge env & token rotation" so new users see the gotcha.

sam: Thanks  once PR is merged please ping me and I'll re-run the harness and clear the flaky flag.
